# Trainctl lifecycle hooks

This directory is a run-local, editable copy of Trainctl's lifecycle hook scripts. Trainctl runs
at most one enabled script per `(callback, modality)` combination, synchronously, on the training
thread, at the actual Lightning callback point, and waits for it to exit before training
continues.

- `light/<callback>.sh` -- cheap: receives a small JSON parameters file describing the callback
  occurrence. Tensor arguments are described (shape/dtype/device), never evaluated.
- `heavy/<callback>.sh` -- expensive: additionally receives NumPy `.npy` exports of any tensor
  arguments supplied to that callback, referenced from a JSON manifest. Files exist only for this
  script's execution and are removed afterward.

Every generated script starts disabled (no execute bit). Enable one with:

    chmod +x hooks/light/on_train_batch_end.sh

Disable it again, without restarting training, with:

    chmod -x hooks/light/on_train_batch_end.sh

Editing or replacing a script takes effect at its next callback occurrence. This copy is
independent of the baseline directory it was seeded from, if any: editing that baseline after
this run starts has no effect on this run, and a deleted script here stays deleted across restarts
of this same run directory.

Catalogue version @@CATALOGUE_VERSION@@: @@CALLBACK_COUNT@@ supported callbacks, @@SLOT_COUNT@@
script slots (light + heavy).

See `trainctl.log` in this run directory for hook discovery, dispatch, and failure diagnostics.
